<%!-- The surface gallery (CLIN-10 finding #15): every declared surface
     in sequence, one section per surface. The phoenix storybook renders
     host HEEx function components — it cannot render an A2UI surface
     (a shadow-DOM wire composition hydrated by the LiveRenderer), so
     the design system's spec page was blind to the layer where the
     anatomy lives. This is the honest complement: each surface in its
     real route, framed, under a presence-style header. Deliberately
     dumb — an iframe per surface, no orchestration — because the
     surfaces are live; anything clever would fight them for events.
     Dev-only by route. --%>
<header class="mb-6">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-display">Surface gallery</h1>
  <p class="text-foreground/70">
    Every declared surface, live — the spec page for the wire compositions the component storybook cannot render. Dev-only.
  </p>
</header>

<section
  :for={{label, route, surface_id} <- @surfaces}
  id={"gallery-#{surface_id}"}
  class="mb-8"
  aria-label={label}
>
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class="mr-2 inline-block size-3.5 -rotate-6 rounded-base border-2 border-border bg-main" aria-hidden="true" />
    {label}
    <span class="ml-2 text-sm font-base text-foreground/60">{route} · {surface_id}</span>
  </h2>
  <%!-- Tall frame per surface: the surfaces are the point, not the
       scroll. Loading=lazy so the page boots without paying for every
       hydration at once. --%>
  <iframe
    src={route}
    title={label}
    loading="lazy"
    class="h-[28rem] w-full rounded-base border-2 border-border bg-secondary-background shadow-shadow"
  >
  </iframe>
</section>
